<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Toggenburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1209 CE – 1468 CE (approx.) · capital Lichtensteig</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">East Swiss county of the upper Thur valley whose last count's death in 1436 set off the Old Zürich War between Swiss confederates.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The lords of Toggenburg appear in the 11th century and are documented as counts by the early 13th century, holding the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thur">Thur</a> valley from castles near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lichtensteig">Lichtensteig</a>. Through marriage and purchase they gained wide lands in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prattigau">Prättigau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/davos">Davos</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts ruled a valley of farmers and herders and fought frequently with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imperial-abbey-of-saint-gall">Imperial Abbey of Saint Gall</a> and with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-vii-count-of-toggenburg">Frederick VII</a> became one of the most powerful lords in the region, allying with both <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Zürich</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-schwyz">Schwyz</a>. Communities in his Rhaetian lands formed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-the-ten-jurisdictions">League of the Ten Jurisdictions</a> after his death in 1436.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-vii-count-of-toggenburg">Frederick VII</a> died childless in 1436, and the rival claims of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Zürich</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-schwyz">Schwyz</a> to his lands caused the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war">Old Zürich War</a> of 1440 to 1446. The core county passed to the barons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raron">Raron</a>, who sold it to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imperial-abbey-of-saint-gall">Imperial Abbey of Saint Gall</a> in 1468.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-toggenburg.jpg" alt="County of Toggenburg" width="320" height="256"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius 09:19, 3 July 2006 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grafschaft_Toggenburg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1209 CE – 1468 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lichtensteig</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frederick VII of Toggenburg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alemannic German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Toggenburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1338&amp;focus=county-of-toggenburg" aria-label="County of Toggenburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4893 518 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Toggenburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5213 774L5219 771"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5219 771h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5213 774h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5213 774h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lichtensteig. <a href="/atlas?year=1338&amp;focus=county-of-toggenburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
